%% Regenerate: mmdc -i diagrams/loop-flow.mmd -o /tmp/loop-flow.png -b white -s 2
%%             magick /tmp/loop-flow.png -quality 90 diagrams/loop-flow.webp
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> Coding: loop triggered
    Coding --> Auditing: session idle
    Auditing --> Coding: findings remain, retry section
    Auditing --> Coding: clean, next section
    Auditing --> PostAction: clean, no section left, post-action enabled
    Auditing --> [*]: clean, no section left
    PostAction --> [*]: post-action complete
    Coding --> [*]: max iterations / 3 consecutive errors / stall timeout / cancellation
    note right of Coding
        Loops start by creating a git worktree, an
        optional msb sandbox, and a code session.
        Plan loops decompose the plan into up to
        24 sections once at start.
    end note
    note right of Auditing
        A section advances only when no bug finding is
        outstanding for it, any earlier section, or
        across sections; when no section is still open,
        a clean audit finishes the loop.
        Same-section retries reuse the previous coder
        and audit sessions; a new section, a recurring
        finding, or an unavailable session starts
        fresh ones.
    end note
    note left of PostAction
        Only when loop.postAction.enabled
    end note
